# frozen-duckdb — PRD Revision-2 shapes: COVERAGE BY INHERITANCE (lane R4)
#
# Determination: all Revision-2 individuals (FR-01..05, NFR-01..04,
# AC-1..4) are typed skos:Concept with skos:inScheme prd: in
# schema/requirements.ttl. The existing shapes graph
# gates/blueprint/requirements-shapes.ttl (lane P12) targets them via
# prd:RequirementShape's SPARQL target (SELECT ?this WHERE { ?this
# skos:inScheme prd: }), so no parallel shape set is needed here — a
# second shapes graph over the same target would double-validate and
# drift. This file is therefore a thin coverage record, NOT a shape set.
#
# What inheritance buys (all enforced by requirements-shapes.ttl):
#   - closed NodeShape with exactly-one prd:status, sh:in("PROPOSED",
#     "PARTIAL_ALIVE", "ALIVE")
#   - exactly-one skos:prefLabel (langString)
#   - prd:AliveConditionalShape: prd:status "ALIVE" without prd:court
#     violates (AliveRequiresCourt idiom)
#
# Validating court (real run, lane R4):
#   pyshacl -s gates/blueprint/requirements-shapes.ttl \
#           -e gates/blueprint/requirements-shapes.ttl \
#           schema/requirements.ttl
#   -> CONFORMS (see receipt in lane R4 report; evidence graph
#      validates against its own shapes as both shapes and data graph).
#
# Non-vacuity: the flip court (temp-copy mutate FR-01 prd:status to
# "ALIVE" without prd:court) was executed and VIOLATED as required —
# the shapes can fail; the pass is not vacuous.

@prefix sh:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix prd: <http://frozen-duckdb.local/ontology/requirements#> .

# Declarative record of the coverage decision (no validation semantics
# on purpose — the enforcing shapes live in requirements-shapes.ttl).
prd:Revision2CoverageRecord a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:message "Revision-2 PRD individuals are validated by gates/blueprint/requirements-shapes.ttl via the skos:inScheme prd: target; this graph adds no constraints by design."@en .
